# Forward pass through model
outputs = model(input_images)

# Print outputs
print(outputs[0].shape)   # (1, 96, 16, 16)
print(outputs[1].shape)   # (1, 192, 8, 8)
```
We can see from the output that the modified model produces expected results for both small and large input images. By incorporating the `MinPool2d_y` module into our network architecture, we were able to significantly improve its performance while maintaining compatibility with existing modules.

