 about how we could improve this model. First, let's take a look at what it does:

It takes an input image `x` and passes it through two convolutional layers (`pw1`, `dw1`) followed by a non-linear activation function (`act1`). Then, it applies a depthwise separable convolution layer (`dw1`) which uses a group size equal to the number of channels in the input image. This means that each channel will be processed independently, allowing for more efficient computation. Next, it applies a second convolutional layer (`pw2`, `bn2`, `act2`) followed by another depthwise separable convolution layer (`dw2`). Finally, it adds back the original input image `y`.

